   "permalink": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeDGPYkS5Oy/",
   "timestamp": "2026-10-03T22:09:20+0000",
   "media_type": "VIDEO",
   "media_product_type": "REELS",
   "caption": "Some of my most used Excel functions, as someone who has spent over 10,000 hours in Excel:\n\n* =XLOOKUP / =INDEX(MATCH()) - Used to look up a specific value and return the corresponding item\n\n* =SUMIFS(Sum Range, Criteria 1 Range, Criteria 1…) - Used to sum a range based on specific criteria\n\n* =COUNTIFS - Same concept as =SUMIFS, but used to count instead of sum\n\n* =XIRR(Values, Dates) - Takes a range of cash flows and corresponding dates to calculate internal rate of return\n\n* =RRI (Number of Periods, Present Value, Future Value) - Used to calculate compound annual growth rate or “CAGR”\n\n* =IF(Logic, True Value, False Value) - Checks for a certain logical condition then returns a value if true or false\n\n* =IFERROR(Value, Value If Error) - Used to make sure an error is not returned, returns a specific value instead of an error\n\nFollow if you found these helpful! Not advice, just educational.",
   "first_seen": "2026-11-13T22:58:00Z"
